# kits.override: TEMPORARY. Use a local checkout of a Kit instead of the pinned download.
#
# One line per Kit:   name   path-to-a-checkout   (relative to the repository root)
# `make fetch` / `make setup` then link .kits/<name> to that folder instead of downloading the pin in kits.lock.
# An empty file (or no file) means every Kit is downloaded at its pin.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS NO LINE TODAY: apps/notes_rust needs the App Context Kit's `adopt` API (a Rust core sharing the context the
# Dart UI opened; AppContext.snapshot() in Dart, AppContext::adopt in Rust). It used to live on an unmerged App Context Kit
# branch, so this file pointed .kits/app-context-kit at a sibling worktree. It is merged and pinned in kits.lock now, so the committed
# state depends on no sibling checkout. To try a local change to a Kit, add a line (name, then a path relative to this folder) and
# run make setup; remove it again before you commit.
